{{!< default}}

{{!-- /training — modules discovered from content. A module IS a
public tag: every training post's primary tag names the module it
belongs to, the tag's description is the module's blurb, and
partials/module-grid.hbs does the discovery. Publish a post with
a new primary tag and a new module card appears here.

The cards render on .training-path: one connected rail, each
module numbered, a connector flowing from every card into the
next — module 1, then module 2, then module 3. --}}

<section class="training-hero outer relative">
    <div class="bg-grid" aria-hidden="true"></div>
    <div class="orb" style="width: 340px; height: 340px; top: -110px; right: -80px;" aria-hidden="true"></div>
    <div class="orb" style="width: 280px; height: 280px; bottom: -120px; left: -60px; animation-delay: -3s;" aria-hidden="true"></div>
    <div class="inner relative">
        <span class="kicker">{{> "icons/layers"}} {{t "Training"}}</span>
        <h1>{{t "Training modules"}}</h1>
        <p>{{t "Self-contained modules that chain into one path — finish a module and the next one is waiting. Each page a step, in reading order."}}</p>
    </div>
</section>

<main id="site-main" class="training-main outer">
    <div class="inner">
        <div class="training-path" data-animate-stagger>
            {{> "module-grid" moduleLimit="30"}}
        </div>
        <div class="training-path-end" data-animate>
            <span class="training-path-end-icon">{{> "icons/rocket"}}</span>
            <h2>{{t "Worked through everything?"}}</h2>
            <p>{{t "Take a structured course next — every one ends with something running in your own org."}}</p>
            <a class="btn" href="{{@site.url}}/courses/">{{> "icons/graduation-cap"}} {{t "Browse courses"}}</a>
        </div>
    </div>
</main>
